{"availability":"available","full":"VamP08/AIOpsAnalyst","name":"AIOpsAnalyst","description":"One triage pipeline for logs, GitHub issues, CI failures and status incidents: deterministic clustering, one LLM verdict per cluster, a rule table decides.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-02T13:29:17Z","updated":"2026-10-11T22:06:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://ai-ops-analyst.vercel.app","topics":["aiops","astro","clustering","drain3","github-issues","incident-management","llm","log-analysis","python","triage"],"demo":"https://ai-ops-analyst.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:05.953Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:05.953Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:05.953Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:44:15.136Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T22:39:05.953Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["ai-ops-analyst.vercel.app: the five outcomes, real cases followed from event to decision, how it was measured, every pile it sorted into, and the live feed.","One triage pipeline for every event stream. Server logs, GitHub issues, failed CI runs and status-page incidents go in; deduplicated clusters with a category, a severity, a confidence and an evidence trail come out, and a policy table decides what happens to each one - a Jira ticket, a Slack message, or a human.","The open-source tools in this space each own one silo: alert managers cluster alerts, issue bots label issues, log tools parse logs. The workflow underneath is the same three steps in all of them, so this builds the workflow once and makes the sources adapters."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/VamP08/AIOpsAnalyst/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ba90a658635a5ea967e6e29e0e48ba5bd4265d893759567e38b2d25d929cd299","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:15.310Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:15.310